{
  "root_cause": "execute_transfer interleaves business logic (balance mutation, ledger recording) with observability calls (emit_transfer_event, emit_failure_alert, record_transfer_attempt), making the core transfer logic hard to read and test in isolation. The transient failure path also leaves the sender debited without a compensating credit, and all side-effect concerns are tangled together in one function.",
  "fix_strategy": "Extract a private _do_transfer helper in transfer_service.py that contains only the balance mutations and ledger calls (record_debit, record_credit) and raises on transient failure. Rename the public execute_transfer to a wrapper that calls record_transfer_attempt before, then calls _do_transfer, and handles success/failure by calling emit_transfer_event or emit_failure_alert respectively — keeping all observability in one place and business logic in another.",
  "files": {
    "code_snippets_v2/invariant_partial_fail/models.py": "UNCHANGED",
